/// Half a month for the month of sale, booked first: the sale reads what has been taken.
// Previous hand-entered depreciation: 478.29 USD on 2025-12-29. v4 derives this from the house parts.

/// Sold, 431,500.00 USD. The closing statement is one flow: the house goes out and the price comes in, and it is paid out
/// in legs: the seller's costs (5% commission and 1.25% of other costs, 26_968.75 USD: a less-item of the sale, so it
/// comes off the price and reduces the amount realized), the loan is paid off (what is left of the principal, settling
/// #loan), tenant B's deposit is credited to the buyer, and the rest is Jamie's.
2025-12-29 buyer -> rental-bank 431_500 USD #sale of house
  - 26_968.75 USD #selling-cost of house
2025-12-29 rental-bank -> home-loan 276_282.05 USD ^loan
2025-12-29 rental-bank -> buyer 2_500 USD #deposit of house
// Proceeds remaining after seller costs, payoff and the buyer credit are retained in rental-bank.

/// The interest on the loan since the first of the month, paid out of the proceeds as well. It is Schedule E interest, not a
/// cost of the sale, so it is a flow of its own and not a leg of the statement.
2025-12-29 rental-bank -> lender 1_450.48 USD #interest of house

/// Tenant B's deposit money is Jamie's again: the buyer took the claim. Released into the rental account.
2025-12-29 deposit-bank -> rental-bank 2_500 USD #transfer

/// The rest of the rental account moves to checking.
2025-12-29 rental-bank -> checking 129_981.33 USD #transfer
